{"id":"mahabharata-7-019","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":19,"title":"एकोनविंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 19 · Second day under Drona: Bhagadatta","summary":{"en":"After the night, Drona resolves to seize Yudhishthira while Arjuna is away, and the Pandavas under Dhrishtadyumna meet him. Bhagadatta on his elephant joins the fighting and Drona throws the army into confusion.","kn":"ರಾತ್ರಿಯ ನಂತರ ಅರ್ಜುನ ದೂರವಿರುವಾಗ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನನ್ನು ಹಿಡಿಯಲು ದ್ರೋಣ ನಿರ್ಧರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಧೃಷ್ಟದ್ಯುಮ್ನನ ನೇತೃತ್ವದಲ್ಲಿ ಪಾಂಡವರು ಎದುರಾಗುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಆನೆಯ ಮೇಲೆ ಭಗದತ್ತ ಹೋರಾಟಕ್ಕೆ ಸೇರುತ್ತಾನೆ; ದ್ರೋಣ ಸೈನ್ಯವನ್ನು ಗೊಂದಲಗೊಳಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"रात के बाद द्रोण अर्जुन के दूर रहते युधिष्ठिर को पकड़ने का निश्चय करते हैं और धृष्टद्युम्न के नेतृत्व में पाण्डव उनका सामना करते हैं। हाथी पर भगदत्त युद्ध में शामिल होता है और द्रोण सेना में भ्रम फैलाते हैं।","te":"రాత్రి తరువాత అర్జునుడు దూరంగా ఉండగా యుధిష్ఠిరుని పట్టుకోవాలని ద్రోణుడు నిశ్చయిస్తాడు; ధృష్టద్యుమ్నుని నాయకత్వంలో పాండవులు ఎదుర్కొంటారు. ఏనుగుపై భగదత్తుడు చేరతాడు; ద్రోణుడు సేనను గందరగోళపరుస్తాడు.","ta":"இரவுக்குப்பின் அர்ஜுனன் தொலைவில் இருக்கும்போது யுதிஷ்டிரரைப் பிடிக்க த்ரோணர் தீர்மானிக்கிறார்; த்ருஷ்டத்யும்னன் தலைமையில் பாண்டவர் எதிர்க்கின்றனர். யானையின் மேல் பகதத்தன் சேர, த்ரோணர் படையைக் குழப்புகிறார்.","ml":"രാത്രി കഴിഞ്ഞശേഷം അർജുനൻ അകലെയായിരിക്കുമ്പോൾ യുധിഷ്ഠിരനെ പിടികൂടാൻ ദ്രോണർ തീരുമാനിക്കുന്നു; ധൃഷ്ടദ്യുമ്നന്റെ നേതൃത്വത്തിലുള്ള പാണ്ഡവർ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ നേരിടുന്നു. ഭഗദത്തൻ ആനപ്പുറത്ത് യുദ്ധത്തിൽ ചേരുന്നു; ദ്രോണർ സേനയെ കുഴപ്പത്തിലാക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.19; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"संशप्तकवधपर्व","titleEn":"Samshaptakavadha Parva (Slaying of the Samshaptakas)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"परिणाम्य निशां तां तु भारद्वाजो महारथः ।\nबहूक्त्वा च ततो राजन्राजानं च सुयोधनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having passed that night, the great chariot-warrior Bharadvaja's son, after speaking at length to King Suyodhana,"}},{"n":2,"text":"विधाय योगं पार्थेन संशप्तकगणैः सह ।\nनिष्क्रान्ते च रणात्पार्थे संशप्तकवधं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"and after Partha had gone out of the battle to kill the Samshaptakas, having made the arrangement with the Samshaptaka bands,"}},{"n":3,"text":"व्यूढानीकस्ततो द्रोणः पाण्डवानां महाचमूम् ।\nअभ्ययाद्भरतश्रेष्ठ धर्मराजजिघृक्षया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona, with his army arrayed, advanced against the great army of the Pandavas, best of the Bharatas, wishing to seize Dharmaraja."}},{"n":4,"text":"व्यूहं दृष्ट्वा सुपर्णं तु भारद्वाजकृतं तदा ।\nव्यूहेन मण्डलार्धेन प्रत्यव्यूहद्युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the eagle array that Bharadvaja's son had made, Yudhishthira countered with an array in the form of a half circle."}},{"n":5,"text":"मुखमासीत्सुपर्णस्य भारद्वाजो महारथः ।\nशिरो दुर्योधनो राजा सोदर्यैः सानुगैः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great chariot-warrior Bharadvaja's son was the beak of the eagle, and King Duryodhana, with his brothers and followers, was its head."}},{"n":6,"text":"चक्षुषी कृतवर्मा च गौतमश्चास्यतां वरः ।\nभूतवर्मा क्षेमशर्मा करकर्षश्च वीर्यवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kritavarma and Gautama Kripa, the best, were its eyes, with Bhutavarma, Kshemasharma and the valiant Karakarsha."}},{"n":7,"text":"कलिङ्गाः सिंहलाः प्राच्याः शूराभीरा दशेरकाः ।\nशका यवनकाम्बोजास्तथा हंसपदाश्च ये ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Kalingas, Sinhalas, easterners, Shurabhiras, Dasherakas, Shakas, Yavanas, Kambojas, and the Hamsapadas,"}},{"n":8,"text":"ग्रीवायां शूरसेनाश्च दरदा मद्रकेकयाः ।\nगजाश्वरथपत्त्यौघास्तस्थुः शतसहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"the Shurasenas, Daradas, Madras and Kekayas stood in the neck, with herds of elephants, horses, chariots and footmen by the hundred thousand."}},{"n":9,"text":"भूरिश्रवाः शलः शल्यः सोमदत्तश्च बाह्लिकः ।\nअक्षौहिण्या वृता वीरा दक्षिणं पक्षमाश्रिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhurishravas, Shala, Shalya, Somadatta and Bahlika, heroes, surrounded by an akshauhini, took the right wing."}},{"n":10,"text":"विन्दानुविन्दावावन्त्यौ काम्बोजश्च सुदक्षिणः ।\nवामं पक्षं समाश्रित्य द्रोणपुत्राग्रगाः स्थिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The two from Avanti, Vinda and Anuvinda, and the Kamboja Sudakshina, with Drona's son at their head, took the left wing."}},{"n":11,"text":"पृष्ठे कलिङ्गाः साम्बष्ठा मागधाः पौण्ड्रमद्रकाः ।\nगान्धाराः शकुनिप्राग्याः पार्वतीया वसातयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the back were the Kalingas, Ambashthas, Magadhas, Paundras and Madrakas, the Gandharas led by Shakuni, the mountain tribes and the Vasatis."}},{"n":12,"text":"पुच्छे वैकर्तनः कर्णः सपुत्रज्ञातिबान्धवः ।\nमहत्या सेनया तस्थौ नानाध्वजसमुत्थया ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the tail stood Karna, son of Vikartana, with his sons, kin and relatives, in a great army with many raised banners."}},{"n":13,"text":"जयद्रथो भीमरथः सांयात्रिकसभो जयः ।\nभूमिंजयो वृषक्राथो नैषधश्च महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Jayadratha, Bhimaratha, Samyatrika, Sabha, Jaya, Bhumimjaya, Vrishakratha and the mighty Nishadha,"}},{"n":14,"text":"वृता बलेन महता ब्रह्मलोकपुरस्कृताः ।\nव्यूहस्योपरि ते राजन्स्थिता युद्धविशारदाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"surrounded by a great force, with the world of Brahma as their aim, stood on top of the array, O king, expert in battle."}},{"n":15,"text":"द्रोणेन विहितो व्यूहः पदात्यश्वरथद्विपैः ।\nवातोद्धूतार्णवाकारः प्रवृत्त इव लक्ष्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The array laid out by Drona with footmen, horses, chariots and elephants looked like a wind-tossed ocean, as if in motion."}},{"n":16,"text":"तस्य पक्षप्रपक्षेभ्यो निष्पतन्ति युयुत्सवः ।\nसविद्युत्स्तनिता मेघाः सर्वदिग्भ्य इवोष्णगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"From its wings and sub-wings, men eager to fight poured out like clouds with lightning and thunder from every direction at the height of summer."}},{"n":17,"text":"तस्य प्राग्ज्योतिषो मध्ये विधिवत्कल्पितं गजम् ।\nआस्थितः शुशुभे राजन्नंशुमानुदये यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the middle of it, Bhagadatta of Pragjyotisha, seated on an elephant arranged by rule, shone, O king, like the sun at its rising."}},{"n":18,"text":"माल्यदामवता राजा श्वेतच्छत्रेण धार्यता ।\nकृत्तिकायोगयुक्तेन पौर्णमास्यामिवेन्दुना ॥","meaning":{"en":"With a garland, with a white umbrella held over him, the king was like the moon at full moon joined with the Krittikas."}},{"n":19,"text":"नीलाञ्जनचयप्रख्यो मदान्धो द्विरदो बभौ ।\nअभिवृष्टो महामेघैर्यथा स्यात्पर्वतो महान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The elephant, blind with rut, like a heap of blue collyrium, looked like a great mountain rained on by great clouds."}},{"n":20,"text":"नानानृपतिभिर्वीरैर्विविधायुधभूषणैः ।\nसमन्वितः पार्वतीयैः शक्रो देवगणैरिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was accompanied by heroic kings of many lands and mountain tribes, with weapons and ornaments of every kind, like Shakra with hosts of gods."}},{"n":21,"text":"ततो युधिष्ठिरः प्रेक्ष्य व्यूहं तमतिमानुषम् ।\nअजय्यमरिभिः संख्ये पार्षतं वाक्यमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Yudhishthira, seeing that superhuman array, unconquerable by foes in battle, spoke to Prishata's son."}},{"n":22,"text":"ब्राह्मणस्य वशं नाहमियामद्य यथा प्रभो ।\nपारावतसवर्णाश्व तथा नीतिर्विधीयताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Arrange such a plan, my lord, that I do not fall under the brahmin's control today, you with the pigeon-colored horses.\""}},{"text":"धृष्टद्युम्न उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhrishtadyumna said:"}},{"n":23,"text":"द्रोणस्य यतमानस्य वशं नैष्यसि सुव्रत ।\nअहमावारयिष्यामि द्रोणमद्य सहानुगम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Though Drona strives, you will not come under his control, steadfast one. I will check Drona today together with his followers."}},{"n":24,"text":"मयि जीवति कौरव्य नोद्वेगं कर्तुमर्हसि ।\nन हि शक्तो रणे द्रोणो विजेतुं मां कथंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"While I live, descendant of Kuru, you should have no fear. Drona cannot defeat me in battle in any way.\""}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":25,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा किरन्बाणान्द्रुपदस्य सुतो बली ।\nपारावतसवर्णाश्वः स्वयं द्रोणमुपाद्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, the mighty son of Drupada, scattering arrows, with his pigeon-colored horses, himself charged at Drona."}},{"n":26,"text":"अनिष्टदर्शनं दृष्ट्वा धृष्टद्युम्नमवस्थितम् ।\nक्षणेनैवाभवद्द्रोणो नातिहृष्टमना इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the unwelcome sight of Dhrishtadyumna standing before him, Drona in an instant seemed not very pleased."}},{"n":27,"text":"तं तु संप्रेक्ष्य पुत्रस्ते दुर्मुखः शत्रुकर्शनः ।\nप्रियं चिकीर्षन्द्रोणस्य धृष्टद्युम्नमवारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him, your son Durmukha, a tormentor of foes, wishing to please Drona, held Dhrishtadyumna back."}},{"n":28,"text":"स संप्रहारस्तुमुलः समरूप इवाभवत् ।\nपार्षतस्य च शूरस्य दुर्मुखस्य च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The clash of the brave son of Prishata and Durmukha was tumultuous, though it seemed an even match, O Bharata."}},{"n":29,"text":"पार्षतः शरजालेन क्षिप्रं प्रच्छाद्य दुर्मुखम् ।\nभारद्वाजं शरौघेण महता समवारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Prishata's son quickly covered Durmukha with nets of arrows, and held Bharadvaja's son back with a great flood of arrows."}},{"n":30,"text":"द्रोणमावारितं दृष्ट्वा भृशायस्तस्तवात्मजः ।\nनानालिङ्गैः शरव्रातैः पार्षतं सममोहयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Drona held back, your son, deeply troubled, bewildered Prishata's son with showers of arrows of many kinds."}},{"n":31,"text":"तयोर्विषक्तयोः संख्ये पाञ्चाल्यकुरुमुख्ययोः ।\nद्रोणो यौधिष्ठिरं सैन्यं बहुधा व्यधमच्छरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"While those two, the leaders of the Panchalas and Kurus, were locked in battle, Drona shattered Yudhishthira's army in many ways with arrows."}},{"n":32,"text":"अनिलेन यथाभ्राणि विच्छिन्नानि समन्ततः ।\nतथा पार्थस्य सैन्यानि विच्छिन्नानि क्वचित्क्वचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As clouds are torn apart on all sides by wind, so the Partha's armies were torn apart here and there."}},{"n":33,"text":"मुहूर्तमिव तद्युद्धमासीन्मधुरदर्शनम् ।\nतत उन्मत्तवद्राजन्निर्मर्यादमवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"For a moment that fight was pleasant to see, but then it went on like madness, without restraint, O king."}},{"n":34,"text":"नैव स्वे न परे राजन्नज्ञायन्त परस्परम् ।\nअनुमानेन संज्ञाभिर्युद्धं तत्समवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Neither their own nor the enemy could be told apart, O king, and the battle went on by guess and by signs."}},{"n":35,"text":"चूडामणिषु निष्केषु भूषणेष्वसिचर्मसु ।\nतेषामादित्यवर्णाभा मरीच्यः प्रचकाशिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"On crest-jewels, gold chains, ornaments, swords and shields, the rays of the color of the sun shone."}},{"n":36,"text":"तत्प्रकीर्णपताकानां रथवारणवाजिनाम् ।\nबलाकाशबलाभ्राभं ददृशे रूपमाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"The look of the battle, with scattered banners, chariots, elephants and horses, was like a sky of cranes and clouds."}},{"n":37,"text":"नरानेव नरा जघ्नुरुदग्राश्च हया हयान् ।\nरथांश्च रथिनो जघ्नुर्वारणा वरवारणान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men killed men, and eager horses killed horses, chariot-warriors killed chariot-warriors, and elephants killed the best elephants."}},{"n":38,"text":"समुच्छ्रितपताकानां गजानां परमद्विपैः ।\nक्षणेन तुमुलो घोरः संग्रामः समवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"In a moment a terrible, tumultuous battle arose among elephants with raised banners and the supreme elephants."}},{"n":39,"text":"तेषां संसक्तगात्राणां कर्षतामितरेतरम् ।\nदन्तसंघातसंघर्षात्सधूमोऽग्निरजायत ॥","meaning":{"en":"As they pressed body to body and dragged one another, from the clash of tusks fire with smoke was born."}},{"n":40,"text":"विप्रकीर्णपताकास्ते विषाणजनिताग्नयः ।\nबभूवुः खं समासाद्य सविद्युत इवाम्बुदाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With banners scattered and fire born from the tusks, they became like clouds with lightning in the sky."}},{"n":41,"text":"विक्षरद्भिर्नदद्भिश्च निपतद्भिश्च वारणैः ।\nसंबभूव मही कीर्णा मेघैर्द्यौरिव शारदी ॥","meaning":{"en":"With elephants bleeding, trumpeting and falling, the earth was strewn as the autumn sky is with clouds."}},{"n":42,"text":"तेषामाहन्यमानानां बाणतोमरवृष्टिभिः ।\nवारणानां रवो जज्ञे मेघानामिव संप्लवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"From the elephants struck by showers of arrows and spears, a roar arose like the thunder of clouds in the deluge."}},{"n":43,"text":"तोमराभिहताः केचिद्बाणैश्च परमद्विपाः ।\nवित्रेसुः सर्वभूतानां शब्दमेवापरेऽव्रजन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some great elephants, struck by spears and arrows, took fright, while others moved toward the sound of all creatures."}},{"n":44,"text":"विषाणाभिहताश्चापि केचित्तत्र गजा गजैः ।\nचक्रुरार्तस्वरं घोरमुत्पातजलदा इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some elephants, gored by tusks of other elephants, cried out terribly like clouds of ill omen."}},{"n":45,"text":"प्रतीपं ह्रियमाणाश्च वारणा वरवारणैः ।\nउन्मथ्य पुनराजह्रुः प्रेरिताः परमाङ्कुशैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Elephants driven back by the best elephants rallied again, uprooted, urged on by the best goads."}},{"n":46,"text":"महामात्रा महामात्रैस्ताडिताः शरतोमरैः ।\nगजेभ्यः पृथिवीं जग्मुर्मुक्तप्रहरणाङ्कुशाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mahouts struck by mahouts with arrows and spears fell from the elephants to the earth, their weapons and goads dropped."}},{"n":47,"text":"निर्मनुष्याश्च मातङ्गा विनदन्तस्ततस्ततः ।\nछिन्नाभ्राणीव संपेतुः संप्रविश्य परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Elephants without men, bellowing here and there, fell on one another like torn clouds."}},{"n":48,"text":"हतान्परिवहन्तश्च यन्त्रिताः परमायुधैः ।\nदिशो जग्मुर्महानागाः केचिदेकचरा इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some great elephants, guided by supreme weapons, bore away the dead and went off in all directions like solitary wanderers."}},{"n":49,"text":"ताडितास्ताड्यमानाश्च तोमरर्ष्टिपरश्वधैः ।\nपेतुरार्तस्वरं कृत्वा तदा विशसने गजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck and being struck with spears, lances and axes, elephants fell in that slaughter, crying out in pain."}},{"n":50,"text":"तेषां शैलोपमैः कायैर्निपतद्भिः समन्ततः ।\nआहता सहसा भूमिश्चकम्पे च ननाद च ॥","meaning":{"en":"As their bodies like mountains fell on every side, the earth was struck, and suddenly trembled and groaned."}},{"n":51,"text":"सादितैः सगजारोहैः सपताकैः समन्ततः ।\nमातङ्गैः शुशुभे भूमिर्विकीर्णैरिव पर्वतैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With elephants brought down together with their riders and banners on every side, the earth shone as if strewn with mountains."}},{"n":52,"text":"गजस्थाश्च महामात्रा निर्भिन्नहृदया रणे ।\nरथिभिः पातिता भल्लैर्विकीर्णाङ्कुशतोमराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mahouts on elephants, their hearts pierced by chariot-warriors with bhallas, fell, their goads and spears scattered."}},{"n":53,"text":"क्रौञ्चवद्विनदन्तोऽन्ये नाराचाभिहता गजाः ।\nपरान्स्वांश्चापि मृद्नन्तः परिपेतुर्दिशो दश ॥","meaning":{"en":"Other elephants, struck by nârâchas, crying like cranes, trampled enemies and friends alike and ran off in the ten directions."}},{"n":54,"text":"गजाश्वरथसंघानां शरीरौघसमावृता ।\nबभूव पृथिवी राजन्मांसशोणितकर्दमा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The earth, covered with floods of bodies of elephants, horses and chariots, became a mire of flesh and blood, O king."}},{"n":55,"text":"प्रमथ्य च विषाणाग्रैः समुत्क्षिप्य च वारणैः ।\nसचक्राश्च विचक्राश्च रथैरेव महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great chariot-warriors, with their chariots, wheeled or wheel-less, were crushed by tusk-tips and thrown up by elephants."}},{"n":56,"text":"रथाश्च रथिभिर्हीना निर्मनुष्याश्च वाजिनः ।\nहतारोहाश्च मातङ्गा दिशो जग्मुः शरातुराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Chariots without chariot-warriors, horses without men and elephants without riders ran off in all directions, afflicted by arrows."}},{"n":57,"text":"जघानात्र पिता पुत्रं पुत्रश्च पितरं तथा ।\nइत्यासीत्तुमुलं युद्धं न प्रज्ञायत किंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here the father killed the son and the son the father, so tumultuous was the battle that nothing could be understood."}},{"n":58,"text":"आ गुल्फेभ्योऽवसीदन्त नराः शोणितकर्दमे ।\nदीप्यमानैः परिक्षिप्ता दावैरिव महाद्रुमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men sank in the mire of blood up to the ankles, like great trees surrounded by blazing forest fires."}},{"n":59,"text":"शोणितैः सिच्यमानानि वस्त्राणि कवचानि च ।\nछत्राणि च पताकाश्च सर्वं रक्तमदृश्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Clothes and armor sprinkled with blood, umbrellas and banners, all looked red."}},{"n":60,"text":"हयौघाश्च रथौघाश्च नरौघाश्च निपातिताः ।\nसंवृत्ताः पुनरावृत्ता बहुधा रथनेमिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Herds of horses, chariots and men were brought down, rolled over and turned again many times by chariot wheels."}},{"n":61,"text":"स गजौघमहावेगः परासुनरशैवलः ।\nरथौघतुमुलावर्तः प्रबभौ सैन्यसागरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The ocean of the army, with the great force of its herds of elephants, the lifeless men as its moss and the tumultuous whirlpools of herds of chariots, shone."}},{"n":62,"text":"तं वाहनमहानौभिर्योधा जयधनैषिणः ।\nअवगाह्यावमज्जन्तो नैव मोहं प्रचक्रिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Warriors seeking victory and wealth plunged into it by the great boats of their mounts and sank, yet did not lose their senses."}},{"n":63,"text":"शरवर्षाभिवृष्टेषु योधेष्वजितलक्ष्मसु ।\nन हि स्वचित्ततां लेभे कश्चिदाहतलक्षणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With warriors rained on by showers of arrows and not yet having the sign of victory, none whose mark was struck down regained his composure."}},{"n":64,"text":"वर्तमाने तथा युद्धे घोररूपे भयंकरे ।\nमोहयित्वा परान्द्रोणो युधिष्ठिरमुपाद्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As that terrible, fearful battle went on, Drona, having bewildered the enemy, rushed at Yudhishthira."}}]}]}